{
  "id": "ss.relic.molt",
  "name": "Molting rhythm",
  "description": "A body leaving its skin: a small bright oval climbing out over the rim of a larger, darker husk that has split wide open behind it, both edges of the split peeled outward into lips. The inside of the husk shows through the split in a mid grey, not black — it is empty, not a hole — and the new body is white going to pale chitin, the brightest thing on the plate, because after a hit you are the thing that got out and nothing can touch you for the moment. The husk is one tilted piece split into two prongs, with the body the wrong size for it and coming out to one side rather than sitting centred in the opening, which keeps it apart from ss.relic.flicker (two equal bodies) and ss.relic.chrysalis (two equal halves with light between) and keeps the dark-ring-grey-ring-bright-centre of a body framed by its hollow — an eye — off the plate. The first pass cut the split narrow and sat the body on top of it: a dark egg with a pearl on it and two curls that read as horns.",
